confusb (0.2.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Connection policy: only the active session reacts (with several users
    logged in), devices that are already known are not offered again, a
    device seen for the first time is offered with a notification ("View
    information" button) and storage drives are opened with the default
    application once mounted (unless GNOME already does it).
  * Show the capacity, partitions and file systems of storage drives.
  * New "Notices" card in the window with the pending offers; opening the
    window withdraws the notifications and the counter on the icon.
  * Split the service and the window into two processes: the service no
    longer loads GTK (about 30 MB instead of 300 MB) and the window leaves
    the memory when it is closed. The service has its own application ID and
    a hidden desktop file (es.masebastia.confusb.servicio.desktop) for its
    notifications. After upgrading, restart the user service:
    systemctl --user restart confusb.service
  * Fix the "About" dialog (the Close button did not respond, the panel was
    cut off), fit the glass dialogs to short windows and keep every vertical
    scrollbar off the content.
  * Raw data boxes: line spacing, horizontal scrollbar, minimum window width.
  * 23 new strings, translated into all the languages.
  * Build-Depends: add the GObject introspection packages used by the tests.

 -- masebastia <msebastia@protonmail.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:03:02 +0100

confusb (0.2.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

